From: disco-flying-wing-fpv
Subject: [PATCH] WifiRegulation peripheral: the Disco's Wi-Fi country and outdoor setting

The Disco sets its Wi-Fi channels and transmit power limits from its
country (Broadcom regulatory domain) and outdoor flag. Its flight program
handles Common.Settings.Country/AutoCountry and
Common.WifiSettings.OutdoorSetting, not the wifi feature that
WifiAccessPoint uses. Add WifiRegulation (country, automatic, outdoor),
its core, and the Disco's controller (published for the Disco only).
---
diff --git a/arsdkengine/src/main/java/com/parrot/drone/groundsdk/arsdkengine/devicecontroller/BebopFamilyDroneController.java b/arsdkengine/src/main/java/com/parrot/drone/groundsdk/arsdkengine/devicecontroller/BebopFamilyDroneController.java
